# Code owners — the reviewers GitHub requires on every pull request.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: `main`'s ruleset sets `require_code_owner_review: true`, and until now the repo had
# no CODEOWNERS at all — `.github/` was gitignored wholesale, so one could not be committed. A code-owner
# requirement with no code owners defined cannot be satisfied by anyone, so a finished PR (#81) sat BLOCKED
# with no route through it. This is that fix.
#
# GitHub semantics worth knowing before editing. Every one of these fails SILENTLY:
#
#   * An entry only takes effect for accounts with WRITE access. Naming someone who has not been added as a
#     repository collaborator does nothing at all — no error, no warning, simply no owner.
#   * An unknown or misspelled username is ignored the same way. There is no validation anywhere.
#   * The LAST matching pattern wins, not the first, so a catch-all belongs at the TOP and any narrower
#     rule goes below it.
#   * GitHub reads this file from a pull request's BASE branch, so a change here only affects PRs opened
#     against a branch that already has it. That is why this arrives on its own branch instead of inside a
#     feature branch — shipping it inside #81 would not have unblocked #81.

